{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A kind is a 32-bit number that every record carries. A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of a kind holds the records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declared with that kind and no others, so one program can hold your routes, another library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"analytics events and a third’s migrations without any of them seeing the others."}]},{"text":"Choosing the number","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Choosing-the-number"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any number other than 0 works. 0 marks an empty slot, and the macros refuse it. The convention is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"four ASCII letters that name the thing, read as one byte each: “rout” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"r","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"u","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"t","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x72","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6F","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x75","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the kind is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x726F_7574","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The letters make it unlikely that two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"libraries pick the same number, and they stay readable in a hex dump of the binary. Swift computes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one for you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let kind = \"rout\".utf8.reduce(0) { $0 << 8 | UInt32($1) }  \/\/ 0x726F_7574"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Give the kind a name for the code that reads it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let routes = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that reads the set for its users keeps the name internal: the macro writes the kind as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number, so its users’ files never need it.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"When two libraries pick the same number","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"When-two-libraries-pick-the-same-number"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No compiler sees every module at once, so nothing can check that a kind is unique. If two libraries","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"choose the same number, their records land in the same set. A record still hands over its value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"only when asked for its own type, so a set of a type your library owns (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Route"},{"text":", not ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"text":")","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"holds only your declarations. Read your records as a type of your own, and a clash costs nothing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but the time to skip the other library’s records.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Writing the kind at each declaration","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Writing-the-kind-at-each-declaration"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" takes the kind as an integer literal. It has to be a literal because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"macro writes it into the binary at compile time; a named constant isn’t visible to the macro:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"That suits a kind used in a few places. A typo in the number puts the declaration in the wrong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set without any error, though."}]},{"text":"Giving your users a macro","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Giving-your-users-a-macro"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A library that asks its users to register things gives them a macro with the kind built in, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"they write ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"text":" and never see the number. The macro lives in a small compiler plugin built on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the LinkerSetsMacroSupport module, whose documentation walks through the plugin, the macro’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"declaration and the package’s targets. The plugin can also require a protocol of every type it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registers, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":" on a type that isn’t an event fails to compile where it’s written.","type":"text"}]}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Declaring a kind"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"kind":"article","title":"Performance","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LinkerSet"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"title":"LinkerSets","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)":{"kind":"symbol","title":"LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declares a record of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"type":"text","text":" whose value is this declaration’s."}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetentry(kind:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"macro"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetEntry"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"kind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"UInt32","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt32V"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Platforms and linking"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect."}],"type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"What the macros refuse"}}}